+# derive the same filename, and the loader for one silently rewrites the bytes
+# the other's replicas are gathering rows out of. Every shared name therefore
+# also carries a checkpoint tag: the first 16 hex chars of sha256 over the
+# served model path plus the rvn_mtp_graft stamp (source, encoder_version,
+# count) read from that same checkpoint's config.json, which is the config
+# patch 0058 gates the grafted draft on. One checkpoint derives one tag, so
+# its replicas keep converging on one file; a different checkpoint, or one
+# whose identity the serving process does not know, gets its own file or the
+# private pinned table. A file whose tag is not ours is refused, never
+# rewritten. (2) registration success is tracked, and any path that does not
+# end in a serving mapping releases the pin through the very handle that took
+# it, before the mapping is closed; pin, alias query and unpin all go to one
+# runtime handle resolved from /proc/self/maps, never to a second libcudart the
+# dynamic linker happens to bind. With the env var unset the allocation path is
